{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#!/usr/bin/python3\n\nimport sys\n\ndef is_good(f, p, k):\n    for i in range(p):\n        if f[(k * i) % p] != (k * f[i]) % p:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef gen(f, p, k, i):\n    if i == p:\n        return is_good(f, p, k)\n    else:\n        ans = 0\n        for j in range(p):\n            f.append(j)\n            ans += gen(f, p, k, i + 1)\n            f.pop()\n        return ans\n\ndef solve(p, k):\n    num = 0\n    used = set()\n    for j in range(p):\n        if j not in used:\n            num += 1\n        i = j\n        while i not in used:\n            used.add(i)\n            i = (i * k) % p\n    exponent = num - (0 if k == 1 else 1)\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    result = 1\n    base = p % MOD\n    while exponent > 0:\n        if exponent & 1:\n            result = (result * base) % MOD\n        base = (base * base) % MOD\n        exponent >>= 1\n    return result\n\np, k = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\nprint(solve(p, k))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <set>\nusing namespace std;\n\nbool is_good(const vector<int>& f, int p, int k) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < p; i++) {\n        if (f[(k * i) % p] != (k * f[i]) % p) {\n            return false;\n        }\n    }\n    return true;\n}\n\nint gen(vector<int>& f, int p, int k, int i) {\n    if (i == p) {\n        return is_good(f, p, k) ? 1 : 0;\n    } else {\n        int ans = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < p; j++) {\n            f.push_back(j);\n            ans += gen(f, p, k, i + 1);\n            f.pop_back();\n        }\n        return ans;\n    }\n}\n\nlong long solve(int p, int k) {\n    long long num = 0;\n    set<int> used;\n    for (int j = 0; j < p; j++) {\n        if (used.find(j) == used.end()) {\n            num++;\n        }\n        int i = j;\n        while (used.find(i) == used.end()) {\n            used.insert(i);\n            i = (i * k) % p;\n        }\n    }\n    long long exponent = num - (k == 1 ? 0 : 1);\n    const long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n    long long result = 1;\n    long long base = p % MOD;\n    while (exponent > 0) {\n        if (exponent & 1) {\n            result = (result * base) % MOD;\n        }\n        base = (base * base) % MOD;\n        exponent >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n    cout << solve(p, k) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.080780778778717e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.0503786799963564e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.158996332786046e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.1605224460363388, -1.311301275563892e-06, -3.58813522325363e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.031175125390291214, -0.25192970037460327, -0.07908307015895844, -3.7788631743751466e-05, -5.006777428206988e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.0892329066991806, -5.960462772236497e-07, 